ield/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "276a712f-2260-5901-9134-cf67e08a10a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-331821" :question/problem "Consider a function $b(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L{b(t)}=B(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L{{e}^{t}b(t)}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.By definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{t}b(t)}&={\\int}_{0}^{\\infty}{{field-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&={\\int}_{0}^{\\infty}{{field-2}}b(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&={{field-3}}\\quad\\text{for }{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{t}b(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{t}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-1)t}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $B(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-1)t}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t=B(s-1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-1>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42c41150-5104-58cc-927b-f55b94529cb2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Order of a Numerical Method By Comparing LTE for Different Step Sizes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3336951a-28a5-5d0a-b7e7-7204ba4f3e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.019" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396345} {:answer/id #uuid "41e98946-67f6-5f1d-8ca5-3c6679f6ea8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.095" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396346} {:answer/id #uuid "0261233f-014a-5f6e-b33a-74781504c710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "